  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The full suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py:392`), a child context copied the parent's whole `default_map`. A map like `{\"foo\": {\"name\": \"mapped\"}}` was therefore searched for `name` at the top level and never found. The child now takes only its own entry: `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_nested_for_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`. It checks that `default_map={\"foo\": {\"name\": \"mapped\"}}` supplies the value for the `foo` subcommand. I didn't run it against the old code to watch it fail first, as CLAUDE.md asks for bug fixes.\n\nI didn't touch `CHANGES.md` or `docs/`, which CLAUDE.md asks to update for user-visible changes.\n\nIf a subcommand has no entry in the parent's map, its `default_map` is now `None`. Before, it silently inherited the parent's map.",
